meta {
  name: a document a run wrote (preview)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/run-document
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  session: {{sessionId}}
  run: 0123456789ab
  path: docs/plan.md
}

docs {
  One document a playbook or workflow run recorded as written, for the run view's preview, also under a dot folder such as .superpowers/. It opens only when a run_step step_end line of that run in the session's own file names exactly this path; a document a step only reads is no record. Never open, recorded or not, in any letter case, checked on the asked path and on its real path: a file named .env, .envrc, .netrc or .npmrc, a name starting with .env. or .env-, a name ending .pem, .key, .p12 or .pfx, and a path with a .git, .aws or .ssh segment; a .git segment anywhere on the absolute real path refuses too. When the run's run_start line carries a workspace fingerprint, the session's current folder must be the run's folder. Otherwise the sandbox and the answer of GET /api/file: real path inside the session's workspace, CSP-sandboxed, the same typed bytes. 400 malformed session or run id, 404 not recorded, another folder than the run's, a secret name, outside, a directory, missing, or no workspace resolved for the session, 413 over caps (2 MB text / 25 MB image), 415 binary.
  
  Fence: host. Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
